This chapter shares only pack, Stock, inventory, catalogue, examine and available feature.

Use the page library.
Use the foundation, battle, party, maps, lettering and sound chapters.

A pack has a potions (number), a cursor (number), a notice (text), a save request (number) and a pc taken (number), a antidotes (number), a balls (number), a moon stones (number), a hp ups (number), a forest antidote (number), a forest potion (number), a forest ball (number), a route stone (number) and a route hp (number) and a shop item (number).
There is a pack called Stock whose potions is 0 and whose cursor is 0 and whose notice is "" and whose save request is 0 and whose pc taken is 0 and whose antidotes is 0 and whose balls is 0 and whose moon stones is 0 and whose hp ups is 0 and whose forest antidote is 0 and whose forest potion is 0 and whose forest ball is 0 and whose route stone is 0 and whose route hp is 0 and whose shop item is 0.

To work out the available feature (text) at a column (number) by a map row (number):
  Let the item be the feature at the column by the map row.
  If Journey's place is "Viridian Forest":
    If the item is "Antidote" and Stock's forest antidote is 1:
      The answer is "".
    If the item is "Potion" and Stock's forest potion is 1:
      The answer is "".
    If the item is "Poke Ball" and Stock's forest ball is 1:
      The answer is "".
  If Journey's place is "Route 2":
    If the item is "Moon Stone" and Stock's route stone is 1:
      The answer is "".
    If the item is "HP Up" and Stock's route hp is 1:
      The answer is "".
  The answer is the item.

The field signs are wording, in that order:
  "TEXT_REDSHOUSE1F_TV" has "There's a movie on TV. Four boys are walking on railroad tracks.".
  "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_OAKSLAB_SIGN" has "OAK POKEMON RESEARCH LAB".
  "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_SIGN" has "PALLET TOWN: Shades of your journey await!".
  "TEXT_ROUTE1_SIGN" has "ROUTE 1: PALLET TOWN - VIRIDIAN CITY".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_SIGN" has "VIRIDIAN CITY: The eternally green paradise".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_MART_SIGN" has "POKE MART: Shop for useful items.".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_MART_SIGN" has "POKE MART: Shop for useful items.".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_POKECENTER_SIGN" has "POKEMON CENTER: Heal your POKEMON!".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_POKECENTER_SIGN" has "POKEMON CENTER: Heal your POKEMON!".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_GYM_SIGN" has "VIRIDIAN CITY POKEMON GYM".
  "TEXT_ROUTE2_SIGN" has "ROUTE 2: VIRIDIAN CITY - PEWTER CITY".
  "TEXT_ROUTE2_DIGLETTS_CAVE_SIGN" has "DIGLETT'S CAVE".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANFOREST_USE_ANTIDOTE_SIGN" has "If a POKEMON is poisoned, use an ANTIDOTE!".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANFOREST_LEAVING_SIGN" has "Leaving VIRIDIAN FOREST. PEWTER CITY ahead.".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_SIGN" has "PEWTER CITY: A stone gray city".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_MUSEUM_SIGN" has "PEWTER MUSEUM OF SCIENCE".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_GYM_SIGN" has "PEWTER CITY POKEMON GYM: LEADER BROCK".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_POLICE_NOTICE_SIGN" has "NOTICE: Report suspicious activity to the police.".
  "TEXT_ROUTE22_POKEMON_LEAGUE_SIGN" has "POKEMON LEAGUE: Front gate".

To work out the inscription (text) for a sign (text):
  If the sign is "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_PLAYERSHOUSE_SIGN":
    The answer is "{Journey's trainer}'s house".
  If the sign is "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_RIVALSHOUSE_SIGN":
    The answer is "{Journey's rival}'s house".
  Let the notice be the field signs for the sign.
  The answer is the notice's wording or else "TRAINER TIPS: Check your POKEMON and items often!".

To examine:
  Let the column be Journey's column.
  Let the map row be Journey's row.
  If Journey's facing is "north":
    Subtract 1 from the map row.
  If Journey's facing is "south":
    Add 1 to the map row.
  If Journey's facing is "west":
    Subtract 1 from the column.
  If Journey's facing is "east":
    Add 1 to the column.
  Let the item be the available feature at the column by the map row.
  If the item is "":
    Stop.
  Set Journey's mode to "dialogue".
  If the item is "Potion":
    Set Stock's forest potion to 1.
    Add 1 to Stock's potions.
    Sound "item".
    Set Journey's message to "Found a POTION!".
    Stop.
  If the item is "Antidote":
    Set Stock's forest antidote to 1.
    Add 1 to Stock's antidotes.
    Sound "item".
    Set Journey's message to "Found an ANTIDOTE!".
    Stop.
  If the item is "Poke Ball":
    Set Stock's forest ball to 1.
    Add 1 to Stock's balls.
    Sound "item".
    Set Journey's message to "Found a POKE BALL!".
    Stop.
  If the item is "Moon Stone":
    Set Stock's route stone to 1.
    Add 1 to Stock's moon stones.
    Sound "item".
    Set Journey's message to "Found a MOON STONE!".
    Stop.
  If the item is "HP Up":
    Set Stock's route hp to 1.
    Add 1 to Stock's hp ups.
    Sound "item".
    Set Journey's message to "Found an HP UP!".
    Stop.
  Set Journey's message to the inscription for the item.

To inventory a key (text):
  If Journey's mode is "walk" and the key is "start":
    Set Journey's mode to "field menu".
    Set Stock's cursor to 0.
    Set Stock's notice to "".
    Stop.
  If Journey's mode is "card":
    If the key is "b" or the key is "a" or the key is "start":
      Set Journey's mode to "field menu".
      Set Stock's cursor to 0.
    Stop.
  If Journey's mode is "party" or Journey's mode is "battle party":
    Record.
    If the key is "b":
      If Journey's mode is "battle party":
        Set Journey's mode to "battle".
      Otherwise:
        Set Journey's mode to "field menu".
      Set Stock's cursor to 0.
      Stop.
    If the key is "up":
      Subtract 1 from Stock's cursor.
      If Stock's cursor is less than 0:
        Set Stock's cursor to Team's count - 1.
    If the key is "down":
      Add 1 to Stock's cursor.
      If Stock's cursor is at least Team's count:
        Set Stock's cursor to 0.
    If the key is "a" and Team's count is more than 0:
      Let the slot be Stock's cursor + 1.
      Let the former be Team's selected.
      Switch to the slot.
      Set Stock's notice to Team's notice.
      If Journey's mode is "battle party" and Team's selected is not the former:
        Set Journey's mode to "battle".
        Respond.
    Stop.
  If Journey's mode is "field menu":
    If the key is "b" or the key is "start":
      Set Journey's mode to "walk".
      Stop.
    If the key is "up":
      Subtract 1 from Stock's cursor.
      If Stock's cursor is less than 0:
        Set Stock's cursor to 4.
    If the key is "down":
      Add 1 to Stock's cursor.
      If Stock's cursor is more than 4:
        Set Stock's cursor to 0.
    If the key is "a":
      If Stock's cursor is 0:
        Set Journey's mode to "party".
        Set Stock's cursor to 0.
        Set Stock's notice to "".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 1:
        Set Journey's mode to "bag".
        Set Stock's cursor to 0.
        Set Stock's notice to "".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 2:
        Set Journey's mode to "card".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 3:
        Add 1 to Stock's save request.
        Set Stock's notice to "SAVE REQUESTED".
      Otherwise:
        Set Journey's mode to "walk".
    Stop.
  If Journey's mode is "bag" or Journey's mode is "battle bag":
    If the key is "b":
      If Journey's mode is "battle bag":
        Set Journey's mode to "battle".
      Otherwise:
        Set Journey's mode to "field menu".
        Set Stock's cursor to 1.
      Set Stock's notice to "".
      Stop.
    If the key is "up":
      Subtract 1 from Stock's cursor.
      If Stock's cursor is less than 0:
        Set Stock's cursor to 6.
        If Journey's town map is 1:
          Set Stock's cursor to 7.
    If the key is "down":
      Add 1 to Stock's cursor.
      Let the last item be 6.
      If Journey's town map is 1:
        Set the last item to 7.
      If Stock's cursor is more than the last item:
        Set Stock's cursor to 0.
    If the key is "a":
      If Stock's cursor is 0:
        If Stock's potions is less than 1:
          Set Stock's notice to "NO POTIONS".
        Otherwise if Combat's starter is "":
          Set Stock's notice to "NO POKEMON".
        Otherwise if Combat's health is less than 1:
          Set Stock's notice to "CANNOT USE".
        Otherwise if Combat's health is at least Combat's maximum health:
          Set Stock's notice to "HP IS FULL".
        Otherwise:
          Add 20 to Combat's health.
          If Combat's health is more than Combat's maximum health:
            Set Combat's health to Combat's maximum health.
          Subtract 1 from Stock's potions.
          Set Stock's notice to "HP RESTORED".
          If Journey's mode is "battle bag":
            Let the old effect count be Score's effect count.
            Set Journey's mode to "battle".
            Respond.
            If Score's effect count is the old effect count:
              Sound "heal".
          Otherwise:
            Sound "heal".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 1:
        If Stock's balls is less than 1:
          Set Stock's notice to "NO POKE BALLS".
        Otherwise if Journey's mode is not "battle bag":
          Set Stock's notice to "USE IN BATTLE".
        Otherwise:
          Capture.
          If Team's result is "caught" or Team's result is "escaped":
            Subtract 1 from Stock's balls.
            Set Journey's mode to "battle".
            If Team's result is "escaped":
              Respond.
          Otherwise:
            If Team's result is "full":
              Set Stock's notice to "PARTY IS FULL".
            Otherwise:
              Set Stock's notice to "TRAINER'S POKEMON".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 2:
        Set Stock's notice to "NO POISON TO CURE".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 3:
        Set Stock's notice to "MOON STONE".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 4:
        Set Stock's notice to "HP UP".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 5:
        If Journey's parcel is 1:
          Set Stock's notice to "OAK'S PARCEL".
        Otherwise if Journey's tm34 is 1:
          Set Stock's notice to "TM34 BIDE".
        Otherwise:
          Set Stock's notice to "NO KEY ITEM".
      Otherwise if Stock's cursor is 6 and Journey's town map is 1:
        If Journey's mode is "battle bag":
          Set Stock's notice to "NOT IN BATTLE".
        Otherwise:
          Set Journey's mode to "town map".
          Set Journey's selection to 0.
          If Journey's place is "Route 1":
            Set Journey's selection to 1.
          If Journey's place is "Viridian City" or Journey's place is "Viridian Mart" or Journey's place is "Viridian Center" or Journey's place is "Viridian School":
            Set Journey's selection to 2.
          If Journey's place is "Route 22" or Journey's place is "Route 22 Gate":
            Set Journey's selection to 3.
          If Journey's place is "Route 2" or Journey's place is "Forest South Gate" or Journey's place is "Forest North Gate":
            Set Journey's selection to 4.
          If Journey's place is "Viridian Forest":
            Set Journey's selection to 5.
          If Journey's place is "Pewter City" or Journey's place is "Pewter Gym" or Journey's place is "Pewter Mart" or Journey's place is "Pewter Center" or Journey's place is "Pewter Museum":
            Set Journey's selection to 6.
          Set Stock's notice to "".
      Otherwise:
        If Journey's mode is "battle bag":
          Set Journey's mode to "battle".
        Otherwise:
          Set Journey's mode to "field menu".
          Set Stock's cursor to 1.
    Stop.
  If Journey's mode is "shop":
    If the key is "b":
      Set Journey's mode to "walk".
      Set Stock's notice to "".
      Stop.
    If the key is "up" or the key is "down":
      Add 1 to Stock's shop item.
      If Stock's shop item is more than 2:
        Set Stock's shop item to 0.
    If the key is "a":
      Let the price be 300.
      If Stock's shop item is 1:
        Set the price to 200.
      If Stock's shop item is 2:
        Set the price to 100.
      If Journey's wallet is at least the price:
        Subtract the price from Journey's wallet.
        If Stock's shop item is 0:
          Add 1 to Stock's potions.
        If Stock's shop item is 1:
          Add 1 to Stock's balls.
        If Stock's shop item is 2:
          Add 1 to Stock's antidotes.
        Sound "item".
        Set Stock's notice to "ITEM BOUGHT".
      Otherwise:
        Set Stock's notice to "NOT ENOUGH MONEY".

To catalogue:
  Fill Screen from 0 by 0 with 160 over 144 as 3.
  Fill Screen from 3 by 3 with 154 over 138 as 0.
  If Journey's mode is "field menu":
    Inscribe "MENU" at 12 by 10.
    Inscribe "POKEMON" at 25 by 27.
    Inscribe "ITEM" at 25 by 43.
    Inscribe "TRAINER" at 25 by 59.
    Inscribe "SAVE" at 25 by 75.
    Inscribe "EXIT" at 25 by 91.
    Let the y be 27 + Stock's cursor * 16.
    Inscribe ">" at 12 by the y.
    Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 119.
  If Journey's mode is "party" or Journey's mode is "battle party":
    Record.
    Inscribe "POKEMON" at 12 by 8.
    If Team's count is 0:
      Inscribe "NO POKEMON" at 12 by 28.
    If Team's count is at least 1:
      Inscribe "{First's species} L{First's level} {First's health}/{First's maximum health}" at 22 by 22.
    If Team's count is at least 2:
      Inscribe "{Second's species} L{Second's level} {Second's health}/{Second's maximum health}" at 22 by 36.
    If Team's count is at least 3:
      Inscribe "{Third's species} L{Third's level} {Third's health}/{Third's maximum health}" at 22 by 50.
    If Team's count is at least 4:
      Inscribe "{Fourth's species} L{Fourth's level} {Fourth's health}/{Fourth's maximum health}" at 22 by 64.
    If Team's count is at least 5:
      Inscribe "{Fifth's species} L{Fifth's level} {Fifth's health}/{Fifth's maximum health}" at 22 by 78.
    If Team's count is at least 6:
      Inscribe "{Sixth's species} L{Sixth's level} {Sixth's health}/{Sixth's maximum health}" at 22 by 92.
    Let the y be 22 + Stock's cursor * 14.
    Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
    Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 110.
    Inscribe "A SWITCH B BACK" at 12 by 128.
  If Journey's mode is "bag" or Journey's mode is "battle bag":
    Inscribe "ITEM" at 12 by 8.
    Inscribe "POTION X{Stock's potions}" at 22 by 19.
    Inscribe "POKE BALL X{Stock's balls}" at 22 by 30.
    Inscribe "ANTIDOTE X{Stock's antidotes}" at 22 by 41.
    Inscribe "MOON STONE X{Stock's moon stones}" at 22 by 52.
    Inscribe "HP UP X{Stock's hp ups}" at 22 by 63.
    If Journey's parcel is 1:
      Inscribe "OAK'S PARCEL" at 22 by 74.
    Otherwise if Journey's tm34 is 1:
      Inscribe "TM34" at 22 by 74.
    Otherwise:
      Inscribe "-" at 22 by 74.
    If Journey's town map is 1:
      Inscribe "TOWN MAP" at 22 by 85.
      Inscribe "CANCEL" at 22 by 96.
    Otherwise:
      Inscribe "CANCEL" at 22 by 85.
    Let the y be 19 + Stock's cursor * 11.
    Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
    Inscribe Stock's notice at 10 by 114.
    Inscribe "B BACK" at 10 by 130.
  If Journey's mode is "card":
    Inscribe "TRAINER CARD" at 12 by 10.
    Inscribe "NAME {Journey's trainer}" at 12 by 32.
    Inscribe "MONEY {Journey's wallet}" at 12 by 49.
    If Journey's badge is 1:
      Inscribe "BOULDERBADGE" at 12 by 70.
    Otherwise:
      Inscribe "NO BADGES" at 12 by 70.
    Inscribe "B BACK" at 12 by 125.
  If Journey's mode is "shop":
    Inscribe "POKE MART" at 12 by 8.
    Inscribe "POTION 300" at 22 by 26.
    Inscribe "POKE BALL 200" at 22 by 42.
    Inscribe "ANTIDOTE 100" at 22 by 58.
    Let the y be 26 + Stock's shop item * 16.
    Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
    Inscribe "MONEY {Journey's wallet}" at 12 by 80.
    Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 100.
    Inscribe "A BUY  B EXIT" at 12 by 122.
